      "title": "Positive real L² operator: genuine square root and energy",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A4",
        "edition": "arXiv:2609.06905v1; Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib",
        "anchor": "Appendix D.1 positive real square-root background; B.10-B.11 scalar defect energy precursor. ASTIS background completion, not printed joint GammaP.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Attributed ASTIS background completion supporting Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang. This real scalar-root construction is ASTIS-authored; it is not the printed joint GammaP, B.11 operator identity or a main theorem."
      },
      "statement": "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space and μ any measure. Let D be a bounded positive real-linear operator on L²(μ;ℝ); positivity includes selfadjointness. There exists a bounded positive REAL operator Γ with Γ²=D, and for EVERY real L² class u, ‖Γu‖²=⟨Du,u⟩ℝ. No CFC instance, complex extension, root, finite/probability measure or finite-dimensional L² is a hypothesis.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space and μ any measure. Let D be a bounded positive real-linear operator on L²(μ;ℝ); positivity includes selfadjointness. There exists a bounded positive REAL operator Γ with Γ²=D, and for EVERY real L² class u, ‖Γu‖²=⟨Du,u⟩ℝ. No CFC instance, complex extension, root, finite/probability measure or finite-dimensional L² is a hypothesis.",
        "No finite/probability measure, finite-dimensional L², nontriviality, CFC/root or conjugation-preservation input.",
        "Pointwise conjugation is antiunitary on complex L² and differs from operator adjoint; its root-preservation and the descent are proved internally."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Positive real L² operator: genuine square root and energy",
          "tex": "\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=D,\\quad\\forall u\\in L^2(\\mu;\\mathbb R),\\ \\|\\Gamma u\\|^2=\\langle Du,u\\rangle_{\\mathbb R}."
        }
      ],
